Stores the detailed execution of a stock movement, especially quantities per Lot / Serial Number / Package, and records the actual “done” quantity during picking or inventory operations.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Detailed picking with lot/serial number assignment
Partial moves and split quantities
Inventory adjustments with lots
Package level operations (put in pack)
Production component consumption with lots
Quality control and traceability
Returns and scrap with lot tracking

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
move_id → stock.move (parent)
product_id → product.product
qty_done (float), reserved_uom_qty / reserved_qty
lot_id → stock.lot (critical for traceability)
package_id, result_package_id (for packaging)
location_id, location_dest_id
owner_id, company_id
state (inherited from move)

Critical Hooks: _action_done, write (qty_done updates), _update_reserved_quantity, lot assignment logic, _check_company
Security: Inherited from stock.move + stock.group_stock_user

RAG Routing Keywords:
stock move line, move line, detailed stock move, picking line, lot move, serial move, qty_done, stock.move.line, lot assignment, package move, inventory line detail, traced move
Related Models (most joined):

stock.move (parent)
stock.lot / stock.production.lot (lot_id)
stock.quant (source & destination)
stock.picking
stock.package
product.product

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
stock.move.line is the execution-level child model of stock.move that records actual qty_done per lot_id, serial, or package for every stock movement. It enables precise traceability, lot/serial tracking, partial picking, packaging operations, and updates stock.quant in real time. Essential for advanced warehouse, manufacturing, and quality processes in Odoo Inventory.